course: dictionary
lesson: 14292
title: Notorious: famous for the wrong reasons
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Notorious» means famous for something bad. When a writer says someone is a notorious thief, the word tells you two things: the person is well known, and what they are known for is bad. Look at the clue words around it, such as thief, robbed or late.
explain: «The bandit was notorious across the whole valley.» The clue is that the whole valley knows him, and he is known for bad deeds. Notorious is close to famous, but it always carries a bad reason. Check by swapping in your meaning: "The bandit was famous across the whole valley for bad deeds" still makes sense.
explain: Notorious can also mean well known for an annoying or dangerous quality, not only for crime. «This road is notorious for accidents.» The road is not a criminal. It is known for causing trouble, so the word warns drivers to take care. «She is notorious for being late» means everyone knows she is always late.
fact: «Notorious» means famous for something bad.
fact: «Notorious» can describe a person, a place or a thing, as in «a notorious criminal» or «a notorious road».
fact: «Notoriously» is the adverb, as in «notoriously difficult»: difficult in a way that everyone knows about.
fact: A good check is to ask whether the sentence describes something bad or annoying. If it does, notorious is the bad kind of famous.
fact: Famous can be good, but notorious is never used for something good.
exercise: «The notorious pirate hid his gold in a cave.» What does notorious mean here? | Very quiet | Lost at sea | *Famous for something bad | Kind and gentle
exercise: «This hill is notorious for slippery mud.» What is the hill known for? | Its lovely flowers | Its great views of the sea | *Being slippery and causing trouble | Being very short
exercise: Ravi says notorious means "very good at football". Why is he wrong? | Notorious means good at football | Notorious means tired | *Notorious is used for bad things, not good ones | He is not wrong, it is the same as famous
test: Which word in «The notorious gang robbed three shops last week» is the clue that the gang is bad? | Gang | Last | *Robbed | Three
test: Maya says, «My brother is notorious for losing his socks.» What does this mean? | He is famous for designing socks | *He is well known for losing his socks, which is annoying | He wears his socks only at night | He has the best socks in town
exam: Which sentence uses notorious correctly? | Notorious is the name of my pet cat. | *The school bus is notorious for arriving late. | The notorious puppy won first prize for being good. | The notorious medal was awarded for kindness.
